{"availability":"available","full":"Fripix/Frirss","name":"Frirss","description":"A modern, self-hosted, customizable web frontend for FreshRSS.","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":79,"forks":6,"created":"2026-05-20T08:55:21Z","updated":"2026-09-30T13:03:09Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":["docker","feed-reader","freshrss","pwa","react","rss","rss-reader","self-hosted","typescript"],"demo":"https://frirss.fripix.ch/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-05T19:22:10.997Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-05T19:22:10.997Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-05T19:22:10.997Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-05T19:22:10.997Z","stars":79,"forks":6}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A self-hosted, customizable web frontend for FreshRSS.","FreshRSS has an excellent engine: solid, self-hosted, great at fetching and storing feeds. Its built-in interface just wasn't for me, and none of the alternatives fit what I wanted — so I built my own.","FriRSS sits on top of FreshRSS through its Google Reader API and replaces only the interface."],"features":["Three panes on desktop, and an installable PWA on mobile with swipe navigation, swipe actions and pull-to-refresh.","Full-text extraction (Readability) when a feed only ships a summary — cached, so re-reads are instant. On a feed set to auto-extract, the next articles are warmed ahead of you, images included, so swiping lands on a…","Offline reading. Articles stay readable without a connection, images included. Favorites and read-later are kept automatically; a one-tap Prepare offline sweep covers the last 30 days across every feed.","Favorites, read-later, read/unread, with all / unread / favorites filters. The unread-only choice is remembered per feed — or, if you prefer, one choice applies to every feed (Preferences → General → Unread filter).","Ticking an article read clears it from the unread list — instantly, in every layout including the compact one. Opening an article leaves its row where it is, so you keep your place; only a deliberate tick removes one.…"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Fripix/Frirss/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"a8fff545ab843e2d9694f3ac41b8582e8dd75f24997b5679662b4cd8eb5b5a73","extractedAt":"2026-10-05T19:22:11.170Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-05T19:22:11.170Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A self-hosted, customizable web frontend for FreshRSS.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Fripix/Frirss/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Then open and create the first account — it becomes the administrator.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Fripix/Frirss/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"hosting","status":"documented","text":"Most self-hosted instances are — on a Docker network, anything your router alone can reach.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Fripix/Frirss/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"a8fff545ab843e2d9694f3ac41b8582e8dd75f24997b5679662b4cd8eb5b5a73","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Fripix/Frirss/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-05T19:22:11.171Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-09-30T13:03:09Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Fripix/Frirss/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-05T19:22:11.172Z","hash":"a8fff545ab843e2d9694f3ac41b8582e8dd75f24997b5679662b4cd8eb5b5a73","originalBytes":19585,"storedBytes":19585,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["freshrss","frirss","article","read","nbsp","feed","one","data","every","proxy","server","cache","instance","preferences","url","api","articles","feeds","file","open","page","per","rather","default","docker","only","same","source","them","unread","what","account","app","back","first","key","next","node","opens","redis","row","says","single","when","which","backend","browser","cannot","directory","everything","mark","never","new","through","top","user","view","where","accounts","address","admini